      "id": "case_mapping",
      "codes": [
        "missing-case-counterparts"
      ],
      "reason": "the generator's glyph set has the lowercase ì î ò ù û ā š and not Ì Î Ò Ù Û Ā Š (seven pairs, listed in FontBakery's message); the face's titles need none of them, and a capital is a new skeleton, which is a generator change"
    },
    {
      "id": "valid_glyphnames",
      "codes": [
        "found-invalid-names"
      ],
      "reason": "build.py names a one-character ASCII key outside its name table after the key itself, so the glyph skeletons.js adds for > is named '>' (the only name FontBakery's message lists; '_' is a valid glyph name); renaming it changes font output and is a build.py change with a version"
    }
